    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0654" n="540" xml:id="pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">438.00/167: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-19T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 19,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 23—10:30 a.m.]<anchor
                            n="92" xml:id="d459-f1"/></dateline></opener>
                <p>127. President Borno has informed me that he intends Abel N. Léger as Haitian
                    member of Claims Commission. Mr. Léger is son of former Haitian Minister to the
                    United States and a lawyer of prominence …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d459-f1" n="92" xml:id="d459-f1-content">
                <p>Text printed from corrected copy received Oct. 24, 1922.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
